.TH LSUSERS 1 "July 2026" "lsusers 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lsusers \- list Linux and macOS user accounts simply
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lsusers
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
lsusers lists Linux and macOS user accounts using the system account database.
By default it lists human users.
.PP
On Linux, human accounts are classified using UID_MIN and UID_MAX from
/etc/login.defs. On macOS, human accounts have UID 500 or greater, do not
start with an underscore, and have a home directory below /Users.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B all
List all users.
.TP
.B human
List human users.
.TP
.B system
List system users.
.TP
.B count
Show user counts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --json
Output JSON.
.TP
.B --csv
Output CSV.
.TP
.B --names
Output usernames only.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.TP
.B --help
Show help.
